  "scope": "All 90 partial-ranking signal settings of S4 with lambda<=1, grouped into 82 (n,r,N) keys. Original S4 files/results remain unchanged. Same anchored 25 Efficient / 35 Sharp candidates; not a Cartesian grid or the proposed adaptive-eta algorithm. No mandatory positive-depth selection filter.",
  "selection": "One candidate per family and (n,r,N), minimizing equal-cell mean validation whole-ranking NLL across 20 independent training/validation draws per signal cell. Signal/beta0 controls sharing (n,r,N) share the same candidate. Every planned calibration fit must complete; zero depth and the inherited Borda fallback are eligible. Exact ties use candidate ID. No true-center error or confirmation outcome is used for selection.",
